From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cappy Ishihara <cappy@cappuchino.xyz>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sun4i: dsi: prevent burst loop delay underflow

The burst-mode instruction-loop delay is stored in a u16 before being
reduced to the hardware field. If the horizontal porch is too short for
the fixed 50-cycle subtraction, the value wraps. The TG5050's 720x1280
mode calculates -34 and consequently programs 4062 into the 12-bit N1
field, which was confirmed by live register readback.

Clamp the delay at zero rather than turning a short porch into an almost
maximum-length delay.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun6i_mipi_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun6i_mipi_dsi.c
index c4d0762..30baa75 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun6i_mipi_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun6i_mipi_dsi.c
@@ -459,9 +459,10 @@ static void sun6i_dsi_setup_inst_loop(struct sun6i_dsi *dsi,
 
 	if (device->mode_flags & MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST) {
 		u32 hsync_porch = (mode->htotal - mode->hdisplay) * 150;
+		u32 clocks;
 
-		delay = (hsync_porch / ((mode->clock / 1000) * 8));
-		delay -= 50;
+		clocks = hsync_porch / ((mode->clock / 1000) * 8);
+		delay = clocks > 50 ? clocks - 50 : 0;
 	}
 
 	regmap_write(dsi->regs, SUN6I_DSI_INST_LOOP_SEL_REG,
